Every face here is the vendor's own released STATIC file, byte for byte — only
the filename is ours. Nothing in this directory is instanced, subsetted or
re-named: Pretendard and D2Coding both carry an OFL Reserved Font Name, which a
modified copy may not keep, and a vendor static is better hinted than anything
an instancer cuts. Refreshing a family is therefore a download, a sha256 check,
and a copy — there is no build step.

The design canvas sets labels and buttons at 500, so each family ships its
vendor Medium beside the four RIBBI faces (Pretendard's too, so a Hangul run in
a 500 label finds a face at its own weight).

A variable font is deliberately NOT shipped: `gpui-pre-wgpu`'s
`cosmic_text_system.rs` shapes with the matched face's own usWeightClass and
rasterizes from a font built at `Weight::NORMAL` with no variation settings, so
one variable face draws every weight at 400 and slants for nothing. The set is
Regular, Bold, Italic and Bold Italic — the four RIBBI faces — and no Medium or
SemiBold, because the matched face's weight is also the weight every fallback
lookup runs at and no system font declares 500 or 600
(app/src/tests/font_fallback.rs holds both lines).

Hangul has no italic in any open font. Pretendard and D2Coding ship upright
only, so an italic run slants its Latin and leaves its Hangul upright.

